# Use package.json scripts

Look at `package.json` before running lint, format, typecheck, build, or any
other maintenance command. If a script already does the job, run that script.
Do not reconstruct the equivalent `npx`, `eslint`, `prettier`, or `tsc` line.

```bash
# BAD - invents a command the repo already wraps
npx prettier --write src/foo.tsx
npx eslint . --fix
tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.web.json

# GOOD
npm run format
npm run lint:fix
npm run typecheck
```

Pass extra args to the script only when the script is written to accept them
and the extra scope is necessary. Prefer the full project script over a
one-file rewrite.

Write a one-off command only when no script covers the task. Say so when you
do.
